      "title": "Timetable Officer (Fixed term 6 months)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002179 Date posted 09/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 06/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 4 (£30,378 - £34,610) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002179.pdf Timetable Officer (Fixed term 6 months) Job description Are you passionate about delivering excellent service and supporting the academic experience at Leeds Beckett University? We are seeking a proactive and organised individual to join our Timetable Office as a Timetable Officer. As a key member of the team, you will: • Provide a comprehensive academic timetabling service, working closely with academic and administrative colleagues to produce full-year timetables for students and staff. • Optimise the use of the University estate and specialist facilities, ensuring our timetable systems and records are accurate and well-maintained. • Offer support, guidance, and training on timetabling and data capture systems, and assist with the production of management reports for key stakeholders. • Contribute to the planning and operation of projects, implement business and system processes, and liaise with software suppliers to resolve issues. We are looking for someone who: • Has experience of timetabling in higher education or a similar environment. • Possesses strong IT skills, with the ability to use corporate databases and analyse data to support business intelligence. • Demonstrates excellent problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and the ability to deliver quality user training. • Is committed to outstanding customer service and can communicate effectively with a range of stakeholders. Join us and help shape the student and staff experience at Leeds Beckett University. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Lee Jones at l.g.jones@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Friday 6th November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
