      "title": "Student Engagement Officer",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002174 Date posted 07/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 26/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 3 (£26,093 - £30,378) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack.pdf Student Engagement Officer Job description Are you passionate about helping students succeed? Do you enjoy uniting data analysis with meaningful student support? Leeds Business School is seeking an enthusiastic Student Engagement Officer to join our team. This hybrid role is based partly at our City Campus and partly from home. Working with attendance and engagement data, you will identify patterns, monitor student participation and proactively contact students who may be at risk of disengagement. Using data to inform your decisions, you will help students access the support they need to maximise their academic success and overall university experience. This is a varied role that combines analytical, administrative and student-facing responsibilities. You will be confident working with data, maintaining accurate records and using insight to guide your work, while also building positive relationships with students and colleagues through regular communication and support. We are looking for someone who is organised, proactive and approachable, with excellent communication skills and a commitment to supporting our diverse student community. Leeds Beckett is committed to creating and maintaining a safe, welcoming and inclusive community that nurtures a culture of respect and consideration for all. We encourage applications from people from all backgrounds and aim to have a workforce that reflects the diversity of our student body and the wider society we serve. Closing Date: Monday 26th October (23.59) Interview Date: Thursday 12th November (this may be subject to change) To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Gareth Robertshaw at G.Robertshaw@leedsbeckett.ac.uk Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
