    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=922973OJCz&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Sustainability Manager",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002169 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£44,746 - £50,253) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support, Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002169.pdf Sustainability Manager Job description We are seeking to appoint an experienced and suitably qualified Sustainability Manager to lead the development, implementation and monitoring of the University's sustainability strategies and associated programmes of activity. The post holder will be responsible for promoting and embedding the principles of sustainability across the University's activities, services and operations, with particular emphasis on improving environmental performance, ensuring regulatory compliance and delivering positive environmental and social outcomes. Working within the Planning & Development section of Estates & Facilities, the post holder will provide professional and technical advice on sustainability matters and will work collaboratively with colleagues across the University, including academic and professional services teams, as well as external agencies and other stakeholders. The role will have responsibility for the continued development and management of the University's ISO 14001 Environmental Management System, ensuring that appropriate systems, policies and procedures are maintained to support effective environmental management and compliance. The post holder will also contribute to the development and delivery of sustainability initiatives associated with the University estate, including new-build and refurbishment projects, environmental standards and assessment schemes, external funding opportunities and opportunities to engage staff and students in sustainability activity. We are looking for someone with: A successful track record of planning, leading and organising sustainability activities across a complex, multi-site environment. You will be able to manage competing priorities, resources and deadlines effectively. The ability to work collaboratively across professional and functional boundaries to promote and embed sustainability throughout an organisation. Well-developed communication and interpersonal skills and be able to use a range of communication methods and techniques to ensure effective, appropriate and customer-focused communication with staff, students, senior colleagues and external stakeholders. Further information This is a key professional role within Estates & Facilities, requiring the post holder to work collaboratively across the University to support the achievement of its strategic sustainability objectives. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate the University's values and to contribute effectively to the University's wider objectives and priorities. If you have the relevant professional experience, knowledge and skills and are committed to supporting the University's sustainability objectives, we would welcome your application. Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=949404OJCz&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator (External)",
      "description": "Job profile skip to job profile skip to job details Search for job Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job details Job reference REQ0002172 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 4 (£30,378 - £34,610) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002172.pdf Program Coordinator (External) Job description Could you be the person who gets more local children swimming, and keeps them coming back? We are looking for a Programme Co-ordinator to lead our Junior Swim Programme at Headingley and grow the community participation and membership around it. Beckett Sport runs the sport and physical activity offer at Leeds Beckett University, from student and performance sport through to junior swimming, athletics and tennis for families across Leeds. Our junior and community programmes are growing, and this role sits at the centre of that growth. You will work closely with our Academy Manager and Programme Co-ordinator (Students), and alongside colleagues in athletics and tennis, so that every participant gets a joined-up experience. In this role you will: • Plan, promote and deliver the Junior Swim Programme, membership schemes and community sport activity, with safety and customer experience at the front of everything you do. • Recruit, induct and support swim coaches, casual staff, volunteers and student employees, building a positive and inclusive team. • Run the administration that keeps the programme working: enrolment, progression, waiting lists, membership records, risk assessments and reporting. • Use participation, retention and customer feedback data to improve what we offer and report on how the programme is performing. • Build partnerships with local schools, clubs and community organisations, creating pathways into volunteering, coaching and leadership for our students. • Work with colleagues across the wider Beckett Sport offer on holiday camps, multi-sport events and promotional campaigns. What we are looking for: • A coaching or instructing qualification in a relevant programme. • Experience of running community-led programmes in a sport and leisure or community development setting, including managing memberships or fitness programmes. • Practical knowledge of health and safety, safeguarding and data protection in a busy sports environment. • Strong communication skills, empathy with customers and colleagues, and the initiative to try new approaches. • Flexibility to work evenings and weekends, when many of our programmes run. In retur n, you will join a supportive team that cares about doing things well, with real scope to shape how our junior and community programmes develop. If that sounds like you, we would love to hear from you. The role is based at Headingley Campus. The role is fully campus based, a vibrant community of both students and colleagues. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Jo Mannion at j.mannion@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Job title Program Coordinator (External) Job reference REQ0002172 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 4 (£30,378 - £34,610) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002172.pdf Job description Could you be the person who gets more local children swimming, and keeps them coming back? We are looking for a Programme Co-ordinator to lead our Junior Swim Programme at Headingley and grow the community participation and membership around it. Beckett Sport runs the sport and physical activity offer at Leeds Beckett University, from student and performance sport through to junior swimming, athletics and tennis for families across Leeds. Our junior and community programmes are growing, and this role sits at the centre of that growth. You will work closely with our Academy Manager and Programme Co-ordinator (Students), and alongside colleagues in athletics and tennis, so that every participant gets a joined-up experience. In this role you will: • Plan, promote and deliver the Junior Swim Programme, membership schemes and community sport activity, with safety and customer experience at the front of everything you do. • Recruit, induct and support swim coaches, casual staff, volunteers and student employees, building a positive and inclusive team. • Run the administration that keeps the programme working: enrolment, progression, waiting lists, membership records, risk assessments and reporting. • Use participation, retention and customer feedback data to improve what we offer and report on how the programme is performing. • Build partnerships with local schools, clubs and community organisations, creating pathways into volunteering, coaching and leadership for our students. • Work with colleagues across the wider Beckett Sport offer on holiday camps, multi-sport events and promotional campaigns. What we are looking for: • A coaching or instructing qualification in a relevant programme. • Experience of running community-led programmes in a sport and leisure or community development setting, including managing memberships or fitness programmes. • Practical knowledge of health and safety, safeguarding and data protection in a busy sports environment. • Strong communication skills, empathy with customers and colleagues, and the initiative to try new approaches. • Flexibility to work evenings and weekends, when many of our programmes run. In retur n, you will join a supportive team that cares about doing things well, with real scope to shape how our junior and community programmes develop. If that sounds like you, we would love to hear from you. The role is based at Headingley Campus. The role is fully campus based, a vibrant community of both students and colleagues. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Jo Mannion at j.mannion@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Send to a friend Apply online"
