rnal examining, audit and other quality-related activity; • Providing authoritative advice and guidance on academic regulations, policies, procedures and the maintenance of academic standards; • Contributing to the review and enhancement of academic quality practices, processes and guidance, informed by sector developments and external expectations; • Coordinating quality-related management information, reports and committee activity within required timescales; • Supporting collaborative provision and partnerships, including due diligence, approval, monitoring, review and annual reporting; and • Sharing good practice, supporting staff development and, where required, overseeing the work of administrative colleagues. About you You will bring experience of working with academic enhancement environments, higher education regulations or quality processes in a complex organisation, together with the judgement and confidence to provide accurate and practical advice. You will be able to build constructive relationships with a wide range of colleagues and partners, manage competing priorities and communicate complex information clearly in writing and in person. Closing date: Friday 13th November 2026 (23:59) To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Dominic Ramsden at D.B.Ramsden@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a 